   "family": "stopping",
   "lens": "when and how the model stops: token cap, loops, end-of-text, answer markers",
   "statement": "A trace can degenerate before it ends, into word strings, a switch to Chinese script or repeated windows, and a degenerate trace almost never ends right. The hazard of this grows with edit size (word strings at 2-3x) and with tokens already generated (median first script switch near token 13,600). So oversized edits, and the late part of very long Think-SFT traces, lose answers. A smaller edit or a shorter trace keeps them. At T 1.0 classic loops are absent.",
