   "lens": "sampling: temperature, top-p, entropy of the next-token distribution, what a vote over samples adds",
   "statement": "Under T 1.0 stopping is a sampled event: at each position the model draws a commit/stop token with a small hazard, so the cap-hit share is a survival probability. RL's top-8 directions add a near-constant logit to that hazard (cap hits 96, 77, 46, 25, 5 along the dial); dose multiplies it. Where the base fails by not stopping (short code tasks, fresh contests) the dial converts unfinished samples, at precision below the base's finished answers.",
